# Background agents check out nested worktrees here. They are full copies of the
# repository living inside it, so an ordinary `git add -A` would stage hundreds
# of megabytes of duplicated tree. Ignoring the directory rather than all of
# `.claude/` leaves room to commit shared settings later.
.claude/worktrees/
